      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name} sorry for the very late response lol, \"Why not just report that as a bug?\" its because it is not a bug, the vrchat website is intended to be like that & even currently it still just says: \"Group Public\" even though it should really say the group name instead. \n\n\"you can more easily avoid those groups.\" yes this is true! you might be able to avoid 1 being a bad actor but what if a new one comes along and does the same thing? cant exactly avoid it if you've not been there before and it becomes a tedious loop that is just annoying to deal with, while you can just avoid group public instances all together it makes vrchat become limited because taking \"Infected\" for example it typically only has a single server so that would make it where you cannot play \"Infected\" (could make your own server but then you need people to join and people are more likely to join larger servers so it takes a long time.)",
