      "value": "This is basically just a duplicate of https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/revise-group-moderation-rights-in-public-instances and it was a bad idea then and is still a bad idea.\n\nNow, not entirely. The group owning a group public DOES need to be more visible so it's easier to avoid or select specific groups, and a group or player that is maliciously using the ability to moderate should be reported.\n\nBut if a group can open a group public instance, any actions taking place there - both those of the group itself, and those of other people, reflect on the group. As such, the group needs to be able to moderate any instance with their name attached. If that is unreasonable, then there should be no such thing as group publics at all.\n\nBut honestly, moderated group publics have been a godsend. Except for trolls. I've watched people walk in, start immediately causing problems, and seconds later get booted. That's why we have group publics. I've only seen a vote to kick pass like ... twice. Too many people not paying attention/idle/click no automatically, or someone could just bring in a few friends with them to weight the vote in their favor.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
